# 113 - aegis-dock-v2 (r60 wave, user feedback 2026-11-13)
# Behavior amendments to the Liquid Glass dock, straight from the user:
#   1. No more automatic hiding: the 4 s idle timer and the 2.4 s nav-peek
#      collapse are gone. The dock stays until the user hides it.
#   2. New hide button on the dock (chevron, aegis_ic_collapse) - the user
#      decides when the chrome goes away.
#   3. Collapsed state moves to the bottom-LEFT CORNER (aligned with the
#      dock's vertical band instead of mid-edge), idle bar widened 5->8dp
#      and swell 9->10dp so it is actually findable; tap/swipe-right
#      recalls.
#   4. Auto-hide only while scrolling: TabObserver.onBrowserControls
#      OffsetChanged tracks the content offset - scrolling down arms a
#      1.2 s idle collapse, scrolling up cancels it and brings the dock
#      back. (Keyboard-owns-the-bottom-edge behavior is unchanged.)
#   5. The URL pill is the address line: it always shows the current page
#      URL (scheme stripped, middle-elided) instead of the page title.
#   6. A horizontal fling on the dock switches tabs (right = previous,
#      left = next) via TabModelUtils.setIndex - the dock swipe mirrors
#      Chrome Android's address-bar swipe.
# Files: AegisDockView.java (behavior), aegis_tokens.xml (sliver dimens +
# aegis_dock_hide string), aegis_ic_collapse.xml (new drawable, registered
# in chrome_java_resources.gni).

